      "message": "Please add minimal documentation to the README explaining how to use the maintenance command. At least mention which script to start.\n\nWhen running it on multiple repositories or a complete site the log shows when a gc starts and finishes including the gc progress messages but the repository name is not logged.\n\nMaybe add it to the start and finish log records:\n```\n2024-12-06 17:40:06,333 [INFO] foo/bar started gc\n2024-12-06 17:40:06,333 [INFO] Started\nEnumerating objects: 9, done.\nCounting objects: 100% (9/9), done.\nDelta compression using up to 8 threads\nCompressing objects: 100% (7/7), done.\nWriting objects: 100% (9/9), done.\nBuilding bitmaps: 100% (2/2), done.\nTotal 9 (delta 1), reused 0 (delta 0), pack-reused 0 (from 0)\n2024-12-06 17:40:06,447 [INFO] foo/bar finished\n```\n\nAdding the `-q/--quiet` option only silences the progress output of the underlying git gc command but not the start and finish lines. Maybe we should add another `-qq` option completely silencing the log ?\n\nHow can I discover the options of the gcplus command from the maintenance command ?\n\nI tried to append the `-h` option\n```\n./gerrit-maintenance.py -d $SITE projects -p All-Users gc -h\n```\nbut that fails with an exception.",
